[ PCUBE: A CUBE IN PERSPECTIVE.  THE ARRAY ONLY MULTIPLIES AND ADDS (FJCC68
[ EQS. 5-7): IT CANNOT DIVIDE BY DEPTH, SO V.CUBE IS AN ORTHOGONAL VIEW.
[ HERE THE PROCESSOR DOES WHAT THE ARRAY CANNOT.  ONCE A FRAME, A CLOCK
[ ROUTINE TURNS THE CUBE'S EIGHT CORNERS BY THE DIALS' ANGLES, AS RXYZ
[ WOULD (Z FIRST, THEN Y, THEN X), DIVIDES EACH BY ITS DISTANCE FROM THE
[ EYE, AND WRITES THE RESULT INTO THE PICTURE'S ITEMS.  THE ARRAY IS LEFT
[ ONLY TO SCALE IT.  IT COSTS THE PROCESSOR ABOUT 9 MS OF EACH 25 MS
[ FRAME, MORE THAN A THIRD OF IT, FOR 8 CORNERS: FOR THE 2,000 POINTS OF
[ FIG. 12 IT WOULD TAKE WELL OVER A SECOND A FRAME.
[ TYPE:  ADEPT ("PCUBE")!   DSPLY (V.PCUBE)!
[        CLOCK (DIALS+1, DI.EX)!   CLOCK (PCUBE+1, PC.EX)!
[ NUMBERS ARE FRACTIONS TIMES 2**14 IN WHOLE 30-BIT WORDS.
[
[ THE PICTURE: THE CUBE'S EDGES, AS V.CUBE DRAWS THEM.  THE ROUTINE
[ REWRITES EVERY ITEM'S POINT EACH FRAME; Z IS KEPT, FOR DEPTH CUEING.
V.PCUBE: TEXT /V.PCUBE/
        LDPS (.68)              [ A LARGER PICTURE SCALE: THE POINTS ARE SMALL
PC.I0:  MOVE (0, 0, 0)          [ THE BACK FACE
        DRAW (0, 0, 0); DRAW (0, 0, 0); DRAW (0, 0, 0); DRAW (0, 0, 0)
        DRAW (0, 0, 0)          [ UP TO THE FRONT, AND ROUND IT
        DRAW (0, 0, 0); DRAW (0, 0, 0); DRAW (0, 0, 0); DRAW (0, 0, 0)
        MOVE (0, 0, 0); DRAW (0, 0, 0)  [ THE THREE EDGES LEFT
        MOVE (0, 0, 0); DRAW (0, 0, 0)
        MOVE (0, 0, 0); DRAW (0, 0, 0)
        RET
[ WHICH CORNER EACH ITEM GOES TO (CORNER = X + 2 Y + 4 Z, 1 FOR +)
PC.IT:  0; 1; 3; 2; 0; 4; 5; 7; 6; 4; 1; 5; 3; 7; 2; 6
[ THE CORNERS, AND WHERE EACH LANDS ON THE SCREEN
VX:     -.35; .35; -.35; .35; -.35; .35; -.35; .35
VY:     -.35; -.35; .35; .35; -.35; -.35; .35; .35
VZ:     -.35; -.35; -.35; -.35; .35; .35; .35; .35
PX:     REPEAT 8.
        0
        ENDR
PY:     REPEAT 8.
        0
        ENDR
PZ:     REPEAT 8.
        0
        ENDR
[
[ THE CLOCK ROUTINE
PCUBE:  0
        MDAR DIALZ              [ SINES AND COSINES OF THE THREE ANGLES:
        JPSR PC.SIN             [ COS A = SIN (A + 1/2)
        ARMD SZ
        MDAR DIALZ
        MDAE'F 20000
        JPSR PC.SIN
        ARMD CZ
        MDAR DIALY
        JPSR PC.SIN
        ARMD SY
        MDAR DIALY
        MDAE'F 20000
        JPSR PC.SIN
        ARMD CY
        MDAR DIALX
        JPSR PC.SIN
        ARMD SX
        MDAR DIALX
        MDAE'F 20000
        JPSR PC.SIN
        ARMD CX
[ THE MATRIX OF RXYZ: RZ RY RX
        JPSR PC.MUL; CZ; CY
        ARMD M00                [ CZ CY
        JPSR PC.MUL; SY; SX
        ARMD T1
        JPSR PC.MUL; SY; CX
        ARMD T2
        JPSR PC.MUL; SZ; CX
        ARMD T3
        JPSR PC.MUL; CZ; T1
        MDAE'N T3
        ARMD M01                [ CZ SY SX - SZ CX
        JPSR PC.MUL; SZ; SX
        ARMD T3
        JPSR PC.MUL; CZ; T2
        MDAE T3
        ARMD M02                [ CZ SY CX + SZ SX
        JPSR PC.MUL; SZ; CY
        ARMD M10                [ SZ CY
        JPSR PC.MUL; CZ; CX
        ARMD T3
        JPSR PC.MUL; SZ; T1
        MDAE T3
        ARMD M11                [ SZ SY SX + CZ CX
        JPSR PC.MUL; CZ; SX
        ARMD T3
        JPSR PC.MUL; SZ; T2
        MDAE'N T3
        ARMD M12                [ SZ SY CX - CZ SX
        MDAR'N SY
        ARMD M20                [ - SY
        JPSR PC.MUL; CY; SX
        ARMD M21                [ CY SX
        JPSR PC.MUL; CY; CX
        ARMD M22                [ CY CX
[ EACH CORNER: TURNED, THEN DIVIDED BY ITS DISTANCE FROM THE EYE
        MDAR'F 8.
        ARMD PC.N
        MDAR'F VX
        ARMD P.VX
        MDAR'F VY
        ARMD P.VY
        MDAR'F VZ
        ARMD P.VZ
        MDAR'F PX
        ARMD P.PX
        MDAR'F PY
        ARMD P.PY
        MDAR'F PZ
        ARMD P.PZ
PC.V:   MDAR'I'X P.VX
        ARMD CRX
        MDAR'I'X P.VY
        ARMD CRY
        MDAR'I'X P.VZ
        ARMD CRZ
        JPSR PC.MUL; M00; CRX   [ RX = M00 X + M01 Y + M02 Z
        ARMD T3
        JPSR PC.MUL; M01; CRY
        MDAE T3
        ARMD T3
        JPSR PC.MUL; M02; CRZ
        MDAE T3
        ARMD RX
        JPSR PC.MUL; M10; CRX   [ RY
        ARMD T3
        JPSR PC.MUL; M11; CRY
        MDAE T3
        ARMD T3
        JPSR PC.MUL; M12; CRZ
        MDAE T3
        ARMD RY
        JPSR PC.MUL; M20; CRX   [ RZ: TOWARD THE VIEWER
        ARMD T3
        JPSR PC.MUL; M21; CRY
        MDAE T3
        ARMD T3
        JPSR PC.MUL; M22; CRZ
        MDAE T3
        ARMD RZ
        ARMD'I'X P.PZ           [ KEPT FOR DEPTH CUEING
[ THE EYE IS 2 UNITS FROM THE CENTRE: A POINT AT RZ IS 1 - RZ/2 AS FAR
[ AS THE CENTRE, AND SHOWS 1 / (1 - RZ/2) AS LARGE.  HALF THAT DISTANCE,
[ 1/2 - RZ/4, IS KEPT, SO THAT IT FITS A HALF-WORD; THEN
[ X ON THE SCREEN = RX / (1 - RZ/2) = RX 2**13 / HALF.
        JPSR PC.MUL; QTR; RZ
        ARMD T3
        MDAR'F 20000
        MDAE'N T3
        ARMD HALF
        MDAR RX
        ARLS 13.
        DIVL HALF
        ARMD'I'X P.PX
        MDAR RY
        ARLS 13.
        DIVL HALF
        ARMD'I'X P.PY
        MDAR PC.N
        MDAE'F'N 1
        ARMD PC.N
        JPLS PC.V
[ WRITE EACH ITEM'S POINT: Z IN ITS COMMAND WORD'S LOWER HALF, X AND Y IN
[ THE HALVES OF ITS SECOND WORD (DSPLY P. 17)
        MDAR'F 16.
        ARMD PC.N
        MDAR'F PC.IT
        ARMD P.IT
        MDAR'F PC.I0
        ARMD P.I
PC.W:   MDAR'I'X P.IT           [ THE CORNER
        ARMD PC.K
        MDAE'F PZ
        ARMD P.T
        MDAR'I P.T
        MDAR'A LOW
        ARMD T3                 [ Z, 15 BITS
        MDAR'I P.I              [ THE COMMAND WORD
        MDAR'A HIGH             [ KEEP ITS OPERATION
        MDAR'O T3
        ARMD'I'X P.I
        MDAR PC.K
        MDAE'F PX
        ARMD P.T
        MDAR'I P.T
        MDAR'A LOW
        ARMD T3                 [ X, 15 BITS
        MDAR PC.K
        MDAE'F PY
        ARMD P.T
        MDAR'I P.T
        MDAR'A LOW              [ Y IN THE LOWER HALF
        MDAR'O'H T3             [ X TURNED INTO THE UPPER HALF
        ARMD'I'X P.I
        MDAR PC.N
        MDAE'F'N 1
        ARMD PC.N
        JPLS PC.W
PC.EX:  NOOP                    [ CLOCK PUTS THE RETURN HERE
[
[ PC.MUL: AR = A TIMES B, TWO FRACTIONS.  CALL:  JPSR PC.MUL; A; B
[ (A AND B ARE THE WORDS' ADDRESSES)
PC.MUL: 0
        MDAR'I'X PC.MUL
        ARMD PM.A
        MDAR'I'X PC.MUL
        ARMD PM.B
        MDAR'I PM.A
        MPYL'I PM.B             [ 2**14 TIMES 2**14
        ARRS 14.
        JUMP'I PC.MUL
[
[ PC.SIN: AR = SIN (PI AR), AR A FRACTION OF PI FROM -3/2 TO 3/2.  IT IS
[ BROUGHT INTO -1/2 .. 1/2 BY SIN (PI X) = SIN (PI (1 - X)), THEN AN ODD
[ POLYNOMIAL OF DEGREE 7 IN X, ITS COEFFICIENTS TIMES 2**11.
PC.SIN: 0
        ARMD PS.X
        MDAE'F'N 20000          [ X - 1/2
        JPAN PS.A
        MDAR'F 40000            [ X >= 1/2: 1 - X
        MDAE'N PS.X
        ARMD PS.X
        JUMP PS.B
PS.A:   MDAR PS.X
        MDAE'F 20000            [ X + 1/2
        JPAN PS.N
        JUMP PS.B
PS.N:   MDAR'F'N 40000          [ X < -1/2: -1 - X
        MDAE'N PS.X
        ARMD PS.X
PS.B:   MDAR PS.X
        MPYL PS.X
        ARRS 14.
        ARMD PS.X2              [ X SQUARED
        MPYL PS.C7
        ARRS 14.
        MDAE PS.C5
        MPYL PS.X2
        ARRS 14.
        MDAE PS.C3
        MPYL PS.X2
        ARRS 14.
        MDAE PS.C1
        MPYL PS.X
        ARRS 11.
        ARMD PS.R               [ KEPT WITHIN A FRACTION: -1 < SIN < 1
        MDAE'F'N 37777
        JPAN PS.UP
        MDAR'F 37777
        JUMP'I PC.SIN
PS.UP:  MDAR PS.R
        MDAE'F 37777
        JPAN PS.LO
        MDAR PS.R
        JUMP'I PC.SIN
PS.LO:  MDAR'F'N 37777
        JUMP'I PC.SIN
PS.C1:  6434.                   [ PI
PS.C3:  -10583.                 [ - PI**3 / 6
PS.C5:  5223.                   [ PI**5 / 120
PS.C7:  -1227.                  [ - PI**7 / 5040
[ WORKING WORDS
SX: 0; CX: 0; SY: 0; CY: 0; SZ: 0; CZ: 0
M00: 0; M01: 0; M02: 0; M10: 0; M11: 0; M12: 0; M20: 0; M21: 0; M22: 0
T1: 0; T2: 0; T3: 0; RX: 0; RY: 0; RZ: 0; HALF: 0
CRX: 0; CRY: 0; CRZ: 0
PC.N: 0; PC.K: 0; P.VX: 0; P.VY: 0; P.VZ: 0; P.PX: 0; P.PY: 0; P.PZ: 0
P.IT: 0; P.I: 0; P.T: 0
PM.A: 0; PM.B: 0; PS.X: 0; PS.X2: 0; PS.R: 0
QTR:    .25
LOW:    77777
HIGH:   77777!H
